ptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Well-executed profile month 1-3: 400-1,000 new followers, 8-15% engagement rate, 15-50 profile views/day. Month 3-6: 1,000-3,000 followers, 20-80 profile views/day, first inbound HNI DMs. Month 6-12: 3,000-8,000 followers, 100-300 profile views/day, 5-20 qualified HNI inbound DMs/month, 2-8 booked meetings/month attributable to LinkedIn. Month 12+: compounding — content library becomes evergreen + LinkedIn Search drives ongoing HNI discovery. Peer benchmark in Hyderabad: top 10% wealth managers have 15K-50K followers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we drive inbound HNI + institutional client enquiries from LinkedIn?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Six mechanisms: (1) Optimised About Us + featured section that clearly signals wealth expertise + credential-density (CFA/CA/CFP/MBA + AUM/portfolio size + client-tier), (2) weekly content that ranks in LinkedIn Search for wealth/investment/tax/estate-planning queries, (3) creator-mode newsletter that HNIs subscribe to (LinkedIn's algorithm push newsletter content across the network), (4) strategic engagement (thoughtful comments) on other senior wealth managers + PE + VC + policy-maker posts, (5) LinkedIn Live + article-driven inbound (deeper content earns deeper trust), (6) DM handling flow — every profile visit converts higher when there's warm content history."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should a banker in Hyderabad publish market commentary daily?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not daily — 3-4 quality posts/week outperforms 7 daily posts on engagement + trust. Content velocity + quality balance: post when there's something meaningful to say. Daily posting often triggers algorithm penalty (repetitive + low-quality signal). Ideal cadence: 3-4 posts/week (mix of market commentary + wealth framework + regulatory + client-story) + 2-3 long-form articles/month + 1-2 LinkedIn Live/quarter. In Hyderabad, top-performing wealth managers post 12-16 quality pieces/month + 100+ meaningful comments/month + 3-5 LinkedIn Live/quarter."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does ITD handle content approval + firm compliance for a regulated banker?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"3-step workflow: (1) ITD content writer drafts + attaches supporting research + risk disclosures + compliance-flagged phrases pre-review, (2) You (and/or your firm's compliance officer) reviews via shared Google Doc or WhatsApp within agreed 24-48hr SLA + approves or requests edits, (3) ITD publishes on approved schedule + monitors comments + escalates any compliance-adjacent DMs to you. This mirrors how internal PR teams at Kotak/HDFC/ICICI/Motilal Oswal typically run content approval — external agency substitutes when in-house team unavailable."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if my firm has restrictions on senior bankers using LinkedIn personally?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Common at large private banks + wealth management firms. Two paths: (1) Firm-approved personal LinkedIn with firm-branded posts only (ITD works within firm brand guidelines + compliance framework), (2) Broader personal thought-leadership on macro + wealth topics that doesn't reference firm products (positions you as industry thinker not firm-employee-marketer). In Hyderabad, senior wealth managers at Motilal Oswal + IIFL Wealth + Nuvama + Edelweiss increasingly follow path 2 — firm brand supported + individual thought-leadership grows independently. ITD advises on the right path based on your firm + role + long-term goals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we track LinkedIn ROI for a Hyderabad wealth manager or banker?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Weekly KPIs: profile views + connection acceptance rate + follower growth + post engagement + inbound DMs + saved content + email/InMail responses. Monthly KPIs: HNI inbound DMs + booked meetings + first-meeting-to-client conversion + LinkedIn-attributed AUM addition + brand-search lift (Google search for your name up). Quarterly: cohort AUM attribution — how much of your quarterly new AUM came from LinkedIn-first buyers. Realistic expectation: 3-6 months for first meaningful attribution + 12-18 months for compounding + full ROI clarity. In Hyderabad, wealth managers see Rs 3-25 crore/year AUM lift LinkedIn-attributed at Growth tier."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does ITD's LinkedIn personal branding differ from a generic social media agency?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"(1) Industry-specific expertise: we know SEBI/RBI/AMFI compliance, wealth-industry vocabulary, HNI buyer psychology, PE/VC peer landscape. (2) LinkedIn-native (not general social): we don't repurpose Instagram content to LinkedIn — LinkedIn algorithm rewards long-form + engagement + community, very different from Reels + carousel. (3) Founder + CXO-facing team: senior consultant handles your account (not a junior social manager). (4) Ghostwriting quality: our content passes for authentic voice — HNIs detect ghost-written content instantly, our writers get voice right. (5) Compliance workflow built-in. (6) Transparent retainer + no ad-spend markup + 6-month MSA with cancellation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do we start LinkedIn personal branding with ITD as a Hyderabad banker?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Free 30-min discovery call. We audit your current LinkedIn profile + benchmark against 3-5 competing Hyderabad wealth managers/bankers at your level + share a customised 90-day plan + tier recommendation + first-30-day content plan within 3 working days. No obligation. If you proceed: 1-week onboarding (voice-capture calls + firm-compliance-alignment + content-approval workflow) + first content live in week 2 + monthly performance review + quarterly business review. Whatsapp us if you'd rather send a message first — we respond within 24 hours."}}]}</script>
